<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3652" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăristŏnīcus</span></b> ,
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀριστόνικος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A son of Eumenes II.</i>, <i>king of
				Pergamus</i>, <i>who carried on war with the
				Romans</i>, <i>but was conquered by the consul M.
				Perpenna</i>, <i>and slain in prison</i>, <i><span class="en">Flor. 2,
			20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 36,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Eutr. 4,
			9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Tyrant of Methymnœ in Lesbos</i>, <i><span class="en">Curt. 4,
			5</span></i> sqq.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
